// Remediation — orphaned temporary component links after in-place output-serial
// regeneration. See km/domains/production/serial-management.md
// ("Regenerated output serial → phantom-complete BOM line").
//
// An unconfirmed `contains` edge (temporary component link) whose parent output
// serial is no longer produced by its batch makes the BOM line read complete
// while the serial dialog shows nothing. The parent-aware `declared_serials`
// query stops *counting* these; this script *removes* the stale edges.
//
// SAFE: only unconfirmed (temporary) links are touched — confirmed genealogy of
// record is never removed. The batch-level sentinel (`_from == Batch/<key>`,
// non-traceable output) is preserved.
//
// Run against the Progress ArangoDB (arangosh / _api/cursor). ALWAYS run the
// DRY-RUN first and eyeball the rows before running the REMOVE.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1) DRY-RUN — list every orphan that would be removed (global).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FOR c IN contains
  FILTER !c.confirmed && c.batch_key != null
  FILTER PARSE_IDENTIFIER(c._from).collection == 'Serial'   // skip Batch/<key> sentinel links
  LET is_current = LENGTH(
    FOR bs IN batch_serial
      FILTER bs._from == CONCAT('Batch/', c.batch_key) && bs._to == c._from
      LIMIT 1
      RETURN 1
  ) > 0
  FILTER !is_current
  RETURN {
    link_key: c._key,
    batch_key: c.batch_key,
    defunct_parent: c._from,
    child: c._to,
    component_key: c.component_key,
    phase_key: c.phase_key
  }

